{{!-- The beta band, at the foot of every Faith Received page.

     One partial rather than a copy per template, because the copy in it
     changes and eleven divergent copies of a status notice is how a site
     ends up telling a reader two different things about the same thing.

     WHAT IT IS FOR. Saying plainly that the project is unfinished, and
     asking for the bug. It deliberately does NOT enumerate what is thin
     any more: that list was a standing promise to keep a paragraph in
     step with the data, which it never was. It claimed the scripture
     index did not cover every collection at a moment when the gap was
     something else entirely.

     THE BUTTON. [data-report-issue] is bound by assets/js/faith-report-
     issue.js, which ships with the theme on every page. Nothing here
     needs a script tag of its own.

     PLACEMENT. Last band before the footer, inside <main>. On the
     landing page it sits between the member CTA and the transparency
     block, which is where it has always been. --}}
<section class="lp-band lp-band--cream lp-beta">
  <div class="container container-narrow">
    <p class="lp-num">Beta</p>
    <p>We are actively working on The Faith Received. We expect there are bugs. If you find one, please tell us so we can make it better.</p>
    <p class="lp-beta-act">
      {{!-- fr-btn, not btn btn-primary. Ian, 2026-09-21: "This
           buttons needs to be in the TFR button style." The Mere O
           pill is the magazine's; the library has its own, and this
           band sits at the foot of every Faith Received page. --}}
      <button type="button" class="fr-btn" data-report-issue>Give Feedback</button>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

{{!-- Library cards use the same reader address contract as ported research. --}}
<script defer src="{{asset "js/page/faith-port-links.js"}}&amp;frv=22fa8b0f2bf4941d"></script>
